{"event_id":"E20000127-1090042","name":null,"merged":false,"episodes":["1090042"],"episode_declared":true,"begin":"2000-01-27 23:00:00","end":"2000-01-28 10:00:00","year":2000,"hazards":["extreme-cold"],"places":["BX","BK","MN","QN","SI"],"harbor":false,"narrative":"Strong and gusty northwest winds combined with well below normal temperatures and produced extremely low wind chill values.Across the Lower Hudson Valley, wind chill values ranged from 25 to 35 degrees below zero, as follows:At Stewart Airport in Newburgh, the lowest wind chill of 35 degrees below zero occurred around 10 am on the 28th when the temperature was 5 degrees above zero and the wind speed was 23 mph.At Westchester County Airport in White Plains, the lowest wind chill of 26 degrees below zero occurred around 4 am on the 28th when the temperature was 9 degrees above zero and the wind speed was 21 mph.Across New York City and Long Island, wind chill values ranged from 20 to 30 degrees below zero, as follows:At JFK Airport in Queens, the lowest wind chill of 30 degrees below zero occurred around 8 am on the 28th when the temperature was 9 degrees above zero and the wind speed was 24 mph.  At LaGuardia Airport, a wind chill of 28 degrees below zero was measured.Across Suffolk County, wind chills ranged from 23 degrees below zero at Farmingdale to 29 degrees below zero at Islip.  At Montauk Pt., a wind chill of 24 degrees below zero occurred.","narrative_damaged":0,"deaths_direct":{"v":0,"s":"ok","src":"ncei-storm-events"},"deaths_indirect":{"v":0,"s":"ok","src":"ncei-storm-events"},"injuries_direct":{"v":0,"s":"ok","src":"ncei-storm-events"},"damage_property":{"v":null,"s":"missing","u":"$","src":"ncei-storm-events"},"damage_crops":{"v":null,"s":"missing","u":"$","src":"ncei-storm-events"},"weather":{"temp_max":{"v":25.0,"s":"ok","u":"F","src":"ghcn-daily","n":"LaGuardia Airport, 2000-01-28"},"temp_min":{"v":9.0,"s":"ok","u":"F","src":"ghcn-daily","n":"Central Park, 2000-01-28"},"rain_daily":{"v":0